/target

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Presentation assets — the "body" (docs/adr/0200-authoritative-vs-presentation-data.md).
# Never in Git: models, textures, audio, shaders, packed assets.
#
# The client loads these from its own local pack at startup and degrades to
# the procedural placeholders already in client code (colored boxes,
# synthesized audio, embedded font) when they are absent, so a fresh clone
# is fully playable and CI stays light. Artists own these out of band
# (separate asset repo or shared folder); release engineering assembles packs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Heavy geometry / textures / audio wherever they live under the client:
/crates/client/assets/models/
/crates/client/assets/textures/
/crates/client/assets/audio/
/crates/client/assets/shaders/
/crates/client/assets/packs/

# Same heavy extensions anywhere else in the tree (catches stray downloads):
*.blend
*.fbx
*.obj
*.dae
*.gltf
*.glb
*.psd
*.xcf
*.kra
*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.flac

# Keep the small embedded placeholder font the build actually includes:
!crates/client/assets/fonts/PandemoniumSans-Regular.ttf
!crates/client/assets/fonts/LICENSE.txt

# Local user content discovered beside the executable at runtime — community
# maps, mods, and packs are not part of the canonical tracked content tree:
/user-maps/
/user-packs/
/mods/

# Editor / OS noise
.*.sw[a-z]
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
